# Location-Based Attendance Management System

A role-based web platform that automates and secures employee attendance tracking using geolocation validation, eliminating fraudulent check-ins from unauthorized locations.

##  Features

- **Role-Based Access Control** — Separate workflows and dashboards for Admin, Supervisor, and Employee roles
- **Geolocation-Based Attendance Validation** — Restricts attendance marking to authorized coordinates, preventing proxy attendance and location spoofing
- **Bulk Employee Onboarding** — Excel-based bulk upload system for fast, scalable employee registration
- **Automated Credential Distribution** — Auto-generates and emails login credentials to onboarded employees
- **Real-Time Data Sync** — Firestore-backed live updates across attendance records and user management

##  System Roles

| Role | Capabilities |
|------|-------------|
| **Admin** | Manage employees, configure authorized locations, view organization-wide attendance reports |
| **Supervisor** | Monitor team attendance, approve/flag anomalies, manage employees under their unit |
| **Employee** | Mark attendance (location-verified), view personal attendance history |

##  Tech Stack

- **Frontend:** React.js, JavaScript
- **Authentication:** Firebase Authentication
- **Database:** Firestore (Cloud Firestore, real-time NoSQL)
- **Geolocation:** Browser Geolocation API for coordinate validation
- **Bulk Operations:** Excel-based parsing for onboarding

##  How It Works

1. **Onboarding:** Admin uploads an Excel sheet with employee details → system bulk-creates accounts and emails credentials automatically.
2. **Location Setup:** Admin configures authorized geo-coordinates (office/work location radius) for attendance validation.
3. **Attendance Marking:** Employee attempts to mark attendance → system captures device geolocation → validates against authorized coordinates → accepts or rejects the request.
4. **Monitoring:** Supervisors and Admins view real-time attendance logs and flag inconsistencies.

##  Installation

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/<your-username>/location-based-attendance-system.git

# Navigate to project directory
cd location-based-attendance-system

# Install dependencies
npm install

# Set up Firebase config
# Create a .env file with your Firebase project credentials:
# REACT_APP_FIREBASE_API_KEY=your_api_key
# REACT_APP_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your_auth_domain
# REACT_APP_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your_project_id
# ...

# Run the app
npm start
```

